# Tayaari Pakki Test Engine - Design System

## Core Design Mandate
This document serves as the single source of truth for all visual decisions in the "Tayaari Pakki Test Engine" app. Every screen, component, color, and icon must strictly adhere to the guidelines set forth here to ensure a cohesive, professional, and culturally resonant learning experience.

## Color Palette
The color system balances focus and calm with distinct, high-contrast actions.
- **Primary:** Deep Ocean Blue (Trust, depth, focus)
- **Secondary:** Forest Green (Growth, correctness, progress)
- **Accent/Highlight:** Terracotta / Sand Gold (Energy, alerts, highlights)
- **Background:** Parchment (Warm, paper-like for comfortable reading)
- **Dark Mode Background:** Charcoal (Deep, eye-strain reducing dark theme)

## Visual Motifs
- **Analog & Academic:** Subtle shadows, rounded cards, and paper-like textures.
- **Clarity First:** Generous whitespace, minimizing cognitive load for test-takers.
- **Directional Indicators:** Clear visual cues for correct/incorrect states, progress bars, and navigation.

## UI Components Direction
- **Buttons:** Filled for primary actions (Submit, Next), Outlined for secondary actions (Skip, Review).
- **Cards:** Slightly elevated with soft rounded corners (12dp to 16dp) to represent questions and options.
- **Icons:** Material Symbols (Filled for active/selected states, Outlined for unselected/informational states).

## Typography & Layout Feel
- **Typeface:** Clean, modern sans-serif paired with clear hierarchical sizes.
- **Readability:** Minimum 16sp for body text (questions and options) to ensure readability during long study sessions.
- **Layout:** Edge-to-edge design with adequate padding (16dp to 24dp margins) to frame content beautifully.

## Overall Mood
Focused, Academic, Trustworthy, and Grounding. The app should feel like a premium digital workbook—not a noisy social feed or a sterile corporate utility.
